#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4beabde4-9391-5c49-9c84-d27f12a8d4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555167} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2743c2-aece-5e37-9fb3-267fd2e06267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{5}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555168} {:answer/id #uuid "c902716a-170b-5f40-8f10-729acf242a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555484} {:answer/id #uuid "f093815e-f75c-565e-9977-6e4693f925d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555591} {:answer/id #uuid "f78f1db4-0d1f-5b54-9cb6-c9929e6bf01f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f093815e-f75c-565e-9977-6e4693f925d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555591} :answer-field/id #uuid "593656c5-9d16-5dfd-b341-863c47c4d9b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "44c4828d-5d0a-5c06-aad5-ea02f733cf44" :question/math-academy-id "q-110476" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43dc20c6-76f4-5f40-a083-a68fff62c7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555144} {:answer/id #uuid "89b8174c-7ba1-5290-9544-eefeb40cdcfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555320} {:answer/id #uuid "9114918e-0981-5c69-81c4-192ab15eea5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555341} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c1d932-65e6-50ad-8efd-0e962ff77a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555561} {:answer/id #uuid "e700ce2b-8be4-5604-877b-03482d66f546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e700ce2b-8be4-5604-877b-03482d66f546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccaad93-79fb-5e66-a9e7-978681d178cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5e29c468-7ba6-5997-83d8-49458f8bde8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-110470" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86341e77-1f57-5302-bb6d-a2c8a5537faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555310} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e23238-bfec-5704-ba16-5d10f1e57bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555432} {:answer/id #uuid "c10d3e1f-2274-5367-bc4b-0e95df0e5a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555465} {:answer/id #uuid "e045873a-b588-5fec-8b66-2507fea13467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555547} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a4fd87-0d62-525b-8e48-73d80e64732e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7a4fd87-0d62-525b-8e48-73d80e64732e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555569} :answer-field/id #uuid "9474a4f7-d9d7-5966-bcd5-2d786ecd797e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7135217a-2b68-531f-be98-4ee4582b3546" :question/math-academy-id "q-36478" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of a vector space $V.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3},{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $V$\n\nII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent\n\nIII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $V$" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is a basis, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors in $V,$ and\n\n- $B$ spans $V.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}({b}_{2}+{b}_{3})+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}){b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3},{b}_{3}\\}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3},{b}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}({b}_{2}+{b}_{3})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2}){b}_{3}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$, the given set is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement III is false since the vector ${b}_{3}$ can't be written as a linear combination of $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\}.$ But then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{3} & ={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}({b}_{1}+{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $B$ is linearly dependent. This would contradict the fact that $B$ is a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f28ba3b-cd1a-5312-a326-475f09817234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555335} {:answer/id #uuid "9f87900c-ac03-59b7-a22f-a27c08d7dcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555384} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4c7e47-2ff6-5628-8a44-4a38609cee4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555457} {:answer/id #uuid "e56fa013-502a-520e-9df9-c0a5b75c47c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555562} {:answer/id #uuid "e896ca90-1179-5ebd-a566-cd9370a85b05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f87900c-ac03-59b7-a22f-a27c08d7dcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555384} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ff39bd5-5f03-5b6f-9a75-e235f7b6ece7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "941b6a8e-c424-5e02-9c9b-4d19cc52c2d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75162" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:=-8{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{1}:=-8{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66e98276-9713-51b2-b083-bc615faf49da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555233} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f35f63-cba0-536a-afe1-17f5848ef3a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555433} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6fbd53-974d-5f48-98f5-31381cab21d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555443} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f83954-18fe-5299-b633-e8c83081d25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555572} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cac527-e61f-5f2f-85b0-59626d9e66db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66e98276-9713-51b2-b083-bc615faf49da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555233} :answer-field/id #uuid "65924cba-b05a-57b8-addb-a6b67c843b8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9a623800-a9e7-562e-b4c1-2e4906af2084" :question/math-academy-id "q-107127" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $2.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{1,t,t+1\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{2}[t]$\n\nII. $2t+1$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{1,t,t+1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{1,t,t+1\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot t+(-1)\\cdot (t+1)=0,\n$$\n\n \nwhere all three coefficients are nonzero, so the set is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n2t+1=0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot t+1\\cdot (t+1).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set is not linearly independent, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064be7dc-c00e-551d-b59c-9b5c0cc3eb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555009} {:answer/id #uuid "79fc7d50-2157-579c-9285-9ef0a16c6060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555283} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7e68b0-ecab-5c63-a1f5-236ebb590064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555412} {:answer/id #uuid "bd519e66-5074-5ce2-a475-b9652a52c6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555449} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f4bed5-b3f8-50de-9ea2-abc0ad3054b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd519e66-5074-5ce2-a475-b9652a52c6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555449} :answer-field/id #uuid "62f65add-d1f7-57d9-bd73-9ef3d190de02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab0273b9-503a-530e-8fea-6b6048661bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-107535" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ So the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the matrix $$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ can't be written as a linear combination of \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nsince all these linear combinations result in matrices with the entry ${a}_{11}={a}_{22}:$\n\n$$\na\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+b\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+c\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & a\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c3fc10-a6da-5b0b-aa7d-90a9bad9247b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555040} {:answer/id #uuid "1d84e348-49ea-5141-a3ac-8bf716deab2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555053} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2fbff4-5712-5066-8565-3259d202df8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555169} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4ff0b0-3679-51c5-bd20-387e6523d247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555176} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8c1ea6-6462-530b-96af-e639af83f207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b8c1ea6-6462-530b-96af-e639af83f207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555203} :answer-field/id #uuid "2283e84f-19db-5b85-af87-63a9f95b5c64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da9b8a15-279d-5af5-bedd-335abf7ae54a" :question/math-academy-id "q-107132" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ over $R$ with degrees at most $3.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\nII. $3t-2{t}^{3}$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot t+{x}_{2}\\cdot {t}^{2}+{x}_{3}\\cdot {t}^{3}=0,\n$$\n\n \nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3t-2{t}^{3}=3\\cdot t+0\\cdot {t}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot {t}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the polynomial $1+t$ can't be written as a linear combination of the set\n$\\{t,{t}^{2},{t}^{3}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "524ac2a6-5a9a-5148-8d1d-5ca5d309098c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555186} {:answer/id #uuid "5ceb10ac-2029-5299-9b2b-f37c6c0e52df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555208} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0366e0-ac17-5dc4-9ef7-d8e912021ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555588} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e1dee4-d755-5dce-9b9a-d2e2a492f1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555597} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f694a6-37e0-5cb0-ad91-f0bb2037328f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ceb10ac-2029-5299-9b2b-f37c6c0e52df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555208} :answer-field/id #uuid "605de236-0714-5f9b-b01a-6122dd1e3831" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f4424f4e-4e2c-59a3-8d15-5c180b952f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107938" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of a vector space $V.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent\n\nII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},w\\}$ is a basis of $V$\n\nIII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{1}+{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent" :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is a basis, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors in $V,$ and\n\n- $B$ spans $V.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $\\{{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent then there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{2}+{x}_{2}{b}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhere at least one of $x$'s is not zero. But then \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+0{b}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $B$ is linearly dependent. This would contradict the fact that $B$ is a basis.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $B$ is a basis of $V,$ it is a maximally linearly independent set of vectors. This means that if we add any new vector to the set, it becomes linearly dependent. Hence, the given set is not a basis for $V.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}({b}_{1}+{b}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1}+{x}_{3}){b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{1}+{b}_{3}\\}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{1}+{b}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}=({x}_{1}-{x}_{3}){b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}({b}_{1}+{b}_{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562400 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561647} {:answer/id #uuid "3ea4d3db-3e0f-5246-9e9e-4b07b0cfdfa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561737} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1e9298-04d9-5141-818c-3600950452a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561893} {:answer/id #uuid "a15c2e45-6e4f-5f3f-a77c-905430031175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561982} {:answer/id #uuid "adbb2e17-3aaa-5c1e-9d3b-42764e417a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15e6ec91-c1bf-5fd4-b22a-68eae1a331c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561647} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bddf8b0-a60d-5d3f-b177-ef56758827de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "125421bb-697b-5db0-9420-c14f51cbf8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-20959" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67535166-0c7e-5160-8989-abee9b724e2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561839} {:answer/id #uuid "9420a97a-1b67-58ee-8e48-ea180d4e1322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561950} {:answer/id #uuid "c9625aa7-0555-551d-ba77-01777f30c63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562083} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d8d7ac-e8e5-5005-8c8b-0a4a33651697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562086} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b95b72-f366-5e7c-8edc-5448f9b86cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9625aa7-0555-551d-ba77-01777f30c63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562083} :answer-field/id #uuid "67278fa9-bfc0-5fba-ae59-83c26db20f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c4f9063-8349-57ea-b235-d134f5cba639" :question/math-academy-id "q-34572" :question/problem "Find $q$, if $2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027b8325-bddf-5f10-927c-27e8a8d93f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561588} {:answer/id #uuid "7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561886} {:answer/id #uuid "91df5346-a42d-5fd9-a5ba-0704fb0cc455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561947} {:answer/id #uuid "c3245f41-6987-5e17-b6c5-0c173f25056e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562072} {:answer/id #uuid "e217e4b1-a0b0-5f52-9881-b8ba9a5204d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b39a89b-9b8d-52a3-9357-588262651bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561886} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8913bcd-9ea3-5176-be5c-767230b5bdc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6154ace2-6af4-581c-9596-72c7ea4a622a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105156" :question/problem "Find $t$, if $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $t$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-4t=-16\\,⟹\\,t=4.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $t$ such that \n $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562449 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02aca304-7b48-53d3-b89a-9ec1254a925a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561589} {:answer/id #uuid "77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561878} {:answer/id #uuid "bb24ab63-f2c2-5312-9f4a-1f89c660eb2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562063} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cf2b8d-50b4-5dea-8cdb-f6d96e285ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562085} {:answer/id #uuid "e9436cfd-df38-58b3-bdb8-5acac9079d34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77982fef-cbd9-5b64-9beb-aef93c81e8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561878} :answer-field/id #uuid "167770ed-e7de-54b6-9bfa-73c5e3df3786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980" :question/math-academy-id "q-105158" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202e7707-594c-5dc6-b642-d0f2a066b531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561670} {:answer/id #uuid "75926ae1-f71f-5fca-920d-fc96549abf2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561873} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ac4430-b766-5ef0-94db-838c49da75cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5y \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562035} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562087} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c2949c-d93d-5056-afd3-68aaf8051b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5y \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9ed7e74-cd82-5c17-8e1e-7e850dab4062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562087} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e2c1a1e-5d57-5327-abb7-fcc53ab8ec5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "897c434c-2b3e-570b-8210-f27b51719e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-20964" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y &=0 \\\\ 2x-10y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000e2b43-7a32-5785-9d4a-cc0099f8dbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561578} {:answer/id #uuid "09a68c36-28bf-56b7-82ce-363a6cd0aec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561611} {:answer/id #uuid "1609e0df-99da-5341-bdc8-02d9d8eee654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561648} {:answer/id #uuid "2813de20-ae90-5665-b4a2-be2d2da6cfd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561689} {:answer/id #uuid "d7582991-42f6-598d-b22f-86bb055d2380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7582991-42f6-598d-b22f-86bb055d2380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562120} :answer-field/id #uuid "90a55e28-fe9d-5f4d-b992-64ed7ca312c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f6e40000-d3bb-5e63-9aa5-9e060c0e21d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105153" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 6\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfb10a9-8436-5e35-b531-240827bbf3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561972} {:answer/id #uuid "a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561994} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9c2754-dc15-56f5-8e26-d514db78cd49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562067} {:answer/id #uuid "d28d263f-fd3b-5140-9893-862b22fa936d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562111} {:answer/id #uuid "eb547a3b-90e6-5909-88af-1af5468ae682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a534e8f3-d655-5502-bc89-53c81026a425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561994} :answer-field/id #uuid "036cd528-ad80-51a8-8b57-1c098a2a1799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105163" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{1} \\\\ 7{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $(-2)$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1} & =-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+2{x}_{2} & =4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ -(3)+3\\left(-\\frac{11}{2}\\right) & =-11 \\\\ -\\frac{33}{2} & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563978} {:answer/id #uuid "19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564004} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564041} {:answer/id #uuid "35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564057} {:answer/id #uuid "de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563978} :answer-field/id #uuid "d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/math-academy-id "q-75642" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563983} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564035} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564078} {:answer/id #uuid "466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564086} {:answer/id #uuid "e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563983} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/math-academy-id "q-105317" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(0)+9(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563972} {:answer/id #uuid "2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564044} {:answer/id #uuid "a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564214} {:answer/id #uuid "de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564319} {:answer/id #uuid "e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564044} :answer-field/id #uuid "e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/math-academy-id "q-157254" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563985} {:answer/id #uuid "14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563998} {:answer/id #uuid "62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564121} {:answer/id #uuid "68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564134} {:answer/id #uuid "8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564134} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-75636" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}=-3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-3{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-3{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570699 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03965f7f-aad0-5609-b9a0-c3fff1316755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570128} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8f4efd-35b9-50e5-ae9a-53500e003509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570224} {:answer/id #uuid "549efc17-626b-5081-9f88-fae5e1e79be3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570273} {:answer/id #uuid "985861dc-7105-595a-8796-0675f996a2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570394} {:answer/id #uuid "9993679c-0ae4-5178-a0c0-8b95af338510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "985861dc-7105-595a-8796-0675f996a2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570394} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a456560-f86f-5faa-9eec-30adf9653504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0f13da88-9214-5888-9868-a4b7f8edacdd" :question/math-academy-id "q-72721" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(B)=-21.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{4}$ (switching the first and the fourth rows). What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-det(B) \\\\  & =-(-21) \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac30f51-6622-5c58-93f3-50a3b53c8c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570141} {:answer/id #uuid "2f953ef4-f453-5c93-9447-a0748ed46ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570205} {:answer/id #uuid "6704cf6c-18b2-5a39-a197-97fa19920324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570305} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f7f56b-8fbf-56ae-91f8-59f7c3e1a778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570465} {:answer/id #uuid "fca72fdf-e0ad-5c57-a47b-0e08014cd557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ac30f51-6622-5c58-93f3-50a3b53c8c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570141} :answer-field/id #uuid "2198884a-3958-5d29-bb71-9b17ea66099a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "620b0d62-bee7-51dc-8bf7-49326cfad693" :question/math-academy-id "q-130735" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-5.$ What is the value of $det(3B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B) &={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=3$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(3B) & ={3}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1019053e-6412-5f44-9e4f-1fe6bb45791a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570151} {:answer/id #uuid "3f798de3-28d5-5ba3-8763-15a3b3141a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570229} {:answer/id #uuid "aa538522-a7b3-5bdf-8c80-5b7f518cd7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570424} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a9117e-d65e-5311-b07f-9d4ca375db48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570447} {:answer/id #uuid "cee50cf1-f6c1-5637-a07f-621c8bbfa6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3a9117e-d65e-5311-b07f-9d4ca375db48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570447} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5ac821f-77cc-50ee-b292-5973c2a64068" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "687e18db-1843-51e7-a8a0-475f4a6d1676" :question/math-academy-id "q-72735" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=80.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{4}:=\\frac{3}{10}{R}_{4}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{10}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{3}{10}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot 80 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45da5c6a-1bde-5117-8afe-03d361230714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570247} {:answer/id #uuid "68fa8711-c3f3-5012-9d1a-fb731bd236f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570309} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6393fe-d927-53da-81a2-0f66da9f7288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570375} {:answer/id #uuid "90deae41-5fa1-5e16-8e84-6b13e063a540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570378} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b642dc-e552-5c4b-8e91-0e291d1d1b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45da5c6a-1bde-5117-8afe-03d361230714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570247} :answer-field/id #uuid "711af9c2-1d4a-5a9f-9a30-ae443b985da0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1f0bc2a-d097-538a-b002-360896d3c91f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130769" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=11.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{4}:=3{R}_{4}$ and ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{4}:=3{R}_{4}$ involves multiplying a row by $3,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $3$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we only have to multiply the determinant by $3.$ Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =3det(A) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c95cd97-d991-586e-9d48-4aceab408e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570179} {:answer/id #uuid "804d6b51-a8c2-5553-b8eb-99abf73a0c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570350} {:answer/id #uuid "9747a53a-fd06-5bad-9209-5355bca6ff7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570390} {:answer/id #uuid "ac341626-a276-5402-9622-674048295496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570430} {:answer/id #uuid "fac8b0ff-2e76-500f-9b69-1448d6083a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c95cd97-d991-586e-9d48-4aceab408e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570179} :answer-field/id #uuid "931b45ae-bf74-5d0e-9144-dd8d9e9c7b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7915d65-a649-5e77-8661-8aa533c4bd16" :question/math-academy-id "q-43045" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=3$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $1$st and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(3) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4243c7f8-2743-5826-8ea3-6ef8e115624e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570236} {:answer/id #uuid "51f3b4fe-201b-5333-b047-b7f366028135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "405" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570269} {:answer/id #uuid "745baa5f-b719-5189-ac4b-4648fef6b3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-405" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570333} {:answer/id #uuid "a334f1d1-81fc-5956-9a40-05a3431dd1e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570413} {:answer/id #uuid "fd773a2d-7538-5011-95fc-7be41b06dcde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd773a2d-7538-5011-95fc-7be41b06dcde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570574} :answer-field/id #uuid "db33a278-5e86-591a-8a62-14279c3317f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f9fbd8ca-7a83-50db-a6d3-a36d5d6ceb97" :question/math-academy-id "q-72746" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(C)=-5.$ What is the value of $det(-4C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C) &={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4C) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =(-64)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123e6b37-f5d0-58a4-a315-71252699ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572335} {:answer/id #uuid "3781813b-d8b2-5b24-921b-dce30178d1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572381} {:answer/id #uuid "49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572405} {:answer/id #uuid "7217c7fb-bda2-5564-844d-cd64e72c50f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572447} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f980f5-230b-530c-bbfe-2be36a54ca2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572405} :answer-field/id #uuid "24809e24-c6b5-5bd7-a31f-2f0864640659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bcf3acb-d9f4-5535-b8d1-de8e7ee2e9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-157235" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3} & =3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6-4-2 \\\\ 9+5-14 \\\\ -3+3+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=3,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25e65798-8cb9-5e6a-90b2-bc96c42a9ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572365} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572413} {:answer/id #uuid "ab29bb3a-73e2-5e1e-8a70-ef9505fc697d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572501} {:answer/id #uuid "dc571830-aa37-5965-b6b0-fb4b6669513b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572558} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8c45cd-d498-500f-8405-f10838f41de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572413} :answer-field/id #uuid "76065098-0f94-561f-87a2-0208d448f13f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3e928130-63ab-538e-924b-5fd72d363a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-42880" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has proportional columns\n\nIII. $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572700 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572357} {:answer/id #uuid "20634a88-ab85-5824-bb75-747bedffe291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572360} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3dde88-c021-53a6-a9b7-fc728d6e08ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572465} {:answer/id #uuid "be14d03c-9132-5936-8238-efc2e8f7723f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572531} {:answer/id #uuid "eb75d285-a0d6-5f8c-a9c2-836a45c2758a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572357} :answer-field/id #uuid "115943c0-4406-5318-97d2-aaaf6a81b1a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7fe1aa9d-37dc-5179-a9aa-2b200892c342" :question/math-academy-id "q-42470" :question/problem "Find $6det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6det(A)-2det(B)=6\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "615f9ea6-bf4a-5c33-97ae-d5fd90fe2025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573546} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1cb320-faf4-519e-bb3a-3b286577e104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573666} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b02fdc-e26c-51d1-84e4-cd2865691519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573724} {:answer/id #uuid "f79ba100-ef34-5438-9bfa-f6eebba5776d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573759} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d4cf0c-57ba-584b-add2-be80a88fd83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "615f9ea6-bf4a-5c33-97ae-d5fd90fe2025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573546} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3bef852-1208-5ae1-a04d-1b9e7cc4e7c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a605eaf-55a3-544d-8186-239316368511" :question/math-academy-id "q-105165" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=2$, which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8(2) & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =15 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-2 \\\\ -2(5)+4(2) & =-2 \\\\ -2 & =-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5+2=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fa005b-1cd6-5081-9086-3952281151c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573461} {:answer/id #uuid "57674894-26ce-5222-bc39-0cec6a625ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573535} {:answer/id #uuid "893ad3db-46c5-5114-a0bf-164fbc2e553c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573603} {:answer/id #uuid "b1679c37-12a9-5a57-8ad6-19234d8f62c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573655} {:answer/id #uuid "e47ed6c4-56c5-56bd-aece-e96f46748978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e47ed6c4-56c5-56bd-aece-e96f46748978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573723} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e982092-3b3a-580a-859e-11cdf69c0b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc7e6aad-0683-5027-b3d4-db532b43dae8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74011" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nHowever, the final equation $0=2$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3612f42b-0a38-5946-b9e8-052f69ef6865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573492} {:answer/id #uuid "6951f3cf-b1cc-52f0-8053-481a177d156d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573552} {:answer/id #uuid "80af8001-4176-59b0-a320-b4d9c58112b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573593} {:answer/id #uuid "95896ab6-b57c-5779-a69a-7fc7f0cae1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573618} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe12096-f5e1-5d5a-bc70-4e3a5e7b7b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6951f3cf-b1cc-52f0-8053-481a177d156d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573552} :answer-field/id #uuid "cea41100-341d-5e9c-b722-4fac6c11f9fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d6a42f32-3ff1-5799-9155-413fd42c36ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-74043" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ -5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 11{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+11{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 & 15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 11 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=1$  into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(3)+3(1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=5$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=1,$ which means \n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=5+3+1=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6134031b-c94b-5e16-8ebb-f4d2f21e15fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583306} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf4e9c2-4a44-500c-a083-88af5a66d87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583357} {:answer/id #uuid "926000a4-09fa-56a1-bbf0-771fcf54bdfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583365} {:answer/id #uuid "94bb07ef-c081-5d56-9833-f4dd92e57239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583367} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8d8eb2-5486-5058-8f1c-8dc5520bdd88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94bb07ef-c081-5d56-9833-f4dd92e57239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583367} :answer-field/id #uuid "d928c6ff-4ba1-59bf-8036-b60cac9bdad6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "337d086b-f73c-5fea-8726-816d0ee2325f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110490" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a10e4f-7c80-5e6c-808a-d7d49b2b76a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583252} {:answer/id #uuid "572c9135-7200-5cdc-a71e-b3517e708b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583292} {:answer/id #uuid "6055955b-5583-5743-98fc-71b4b9e5d9fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583305} {:answer/id #uuid "761d35bb-58bc-5ed5-a92c-b034f64cb50e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583323} {:answer/id #uuid "8db76056-c219-58f0-ab0e-f3665bb6854d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "572c9135-7200-5cdc-a71e-b3517e708b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583292} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a05bbf-716e-54f0-95c8-efaacdb15689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c3ad9195-1cab-531c-87e4-5d2ddaeacb6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110479" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583649 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0153544a-8c32-58ed-94d4-ab415c418fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583173} {:answer/id #uuid "395e1cbb-172f-523b-a004-b0c4578f1b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583254} {:answer/id #uuid "8e012bd0-1596-5e67-8851-58bbe3828c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583359} {:answer/id #uuid "adfacaee-3a35-5050-bc6c-9d1e53e20d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583400} {:answer/id #uuid "e1105902-11ed-5384-82e3-92d690406bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e012bd0-1596-5e67-8851-58bbe3828c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583359} :answer-field/id #uuid "7979ea63-e38f-5960-a8b9-f880a691bb58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186583548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e11dd4b2-8bce-5dee-96bc-7cd645b420f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42539" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dcc281-2954-553e-85df-b2f0a146b6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596115} {:answer/id #uuid "5b63239f-68b4-56e6-908b-40798eb8c95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596225} {:answer/id #uuid "67c91ea2-823f-55f4-ad73-17c18ecb13e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596249} {:answer/id #uuid "872cf26f-b537-5f5a-b6b4-14bd0df480ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596296} {:answer/id #uuid "89c446c9-afb0-567e-8891-168dda7e77ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67c91ea2-823f-55f4-ad73-17c18ecb13e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596249} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de0975b-c189-5b10-aee7-198b7786f2cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "063aeb47-cc32-5866-89d5-e236fc5f0c86" :question/math-academy-id "q-74980" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ ${a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -5 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"}]}
